\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a complex square matrix $A$, its numerical range is $W(A)=\{\langle Av,v\rangle:\|v\|=1\}$. If $f$ is analytic on a neighborhood of $W(A)$, must
\[\|f(A)\|\leq2\max_{z\in W(A)}|f(z)|\]
hold in the Euclidean operator norm? The proposed constant is independent of matrix size.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.1016/j.laa.2006.10.013}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does the numerical range control every analytic matrix function with universal constant two?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 1300 (ALG-004). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.1016/j.laa.2006.10.013}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:1300}

